<section id="problem" class="nu-section nu-dark"><span class="nu-index">01</span><div class="nu-wrap nu-grid"><div class="nu-copy nu-reveal"><div class="nu-k">The Problem</div><h2 class="nu-h2 nu-serif">AI was supposed to make life easier.</h2><p class="nu-p">Instead, people often become the manager of the intelligence. AI forgets context, repeats mistakes, loses state, produces things that look finished and makes the human responsible for checking everything.</p><div class="nu-quote">“If you have to constantly manage the intelligence, is it really working for you?”</div></div><div class="nu-media nu-reveal"><img src="https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1MhbTLZRwC1bQwvsKir4LWacsWkH-E-dF&amp;sz=w2200" alt="Shawn Vibert"></div></div></section>

